{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462505-do-the-affects-of-blood-bonding-work-if-the-kindred-is-in-torpor","id":1462505,"title":"Do the Affects of Blood Bonding Work if the Kindred is in Torpor?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-02T18:58:28-07:00","id":1462505,"title":"Do the Affects of Blood Bonding Work if the Kindred is in Torpor?","content":"For instance, say one kindred has another kindred staked in his basement and drinks from them. Does that kindred need to worry about the affects of the bond while the other is staked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T19:48:39-07:00","id":1462507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462505-do-the-affects-of-blood-bonding-work-if-the-kindred-is-in-torpor#post1462505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, say one kindred has another kindred staked in his basement and drinks from them. Does that kindred need to worry about the affects of the bond while the other is staked?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If there's vitae in the torpid kindred to be consumed, i'd say yes, definitely.<br /> <br /> That kindred - unless if possessed of 6+ Animalism, Auspex, Dominate or Presence - might not be in condition to <i>consciously exploit</i> such a bond, but a budding sentiment of devotion/love/loyalty/worshipfulness for the torpid kindred will certainly develop.<br /> <br /> A twisted sort of attachment to the sleeping one and its wellbeing that could go into all sorts of peculiar directions depending on their previous relationship and how much the &quot;drinker&quot; actually knows or not of the sleeper, its mind, likes, dislikes, allies, rivals &amp; etc.<br /> <br /> That said, i can definitely see some individual neonate, ancilla or even elder theorizing that a kindred's vitae might be somewhat inert, attempt exactly that and slowly develop the bond and some sort of fondness without being quite conscious of it because it has one's &quot;paramour&quot; in a handy box close by and safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-02-2021, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T21:19:07-07:00","id":1462511,"title":"","content":"Devoted servants of the vampire trying to resurrect a torpored vampire is a common trope in vampire fiction. I'd say the bond should still exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T23:02:12-07:00","id":1462517,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not. The blood bond isn't a consciously activated power. It's part and parcel of drinking another vampire's vitae.<br /> <br /> Whether the bond is enough to get the staked vampire out of trouble is another question. <i>Gehenna</i> had a fun scenario with a zealous priest (I think also a hunter?) who'd chained up a vampire in his basement, drained her enough times to become fully bonded, and he still kept her chained up. The bond just made him madly possessive and might have also kept him from killing her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":". 10-03-2021, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T00:05:50-07:00","id":1462524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462505-do-the-affects-of-blood-bonding-work-if-the-kindred-is-in-torpor?p=1462517#post1462517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why not. The blood bond isn't a consciously activated power. It's part and parcel of drinking another vampire's vitae.<br /> <br /> Whether the bond is enough to get the staked vampire out of trouble is another question. <i>Gehenna</i> had a fun scenario with a zealous priest (I think also a hunter?) who'd chained up a vampire in his basement, drained her enough times to become fully bonded, and he still kept her chained up. The bond just must made him madly possessive and might have also kept him from killing her.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The kind of situation that could lead into &quot;the Bond loses its power when one is staked and enters torpor&quot; misreading of anecdotal evidence previously discussed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T21:11:55-07:00","id":1462610,"title":"","content":"I would say yes, absolutely. This is one reason why having a Methuselah\u2019s Thirst is so inconvenient, you eventually end up having to kill vampires. If you could just get one vampire, or embrace one, then stake them or beat them into torpor, then you\u2019d have an infinite sources of vampire vitae. The same goes for independent ghouls.<br /> <br /> But this isn\u2019t possible, because the blood bond will develop and then you\u2019ll most likely do what ever you need to revive your slumbering beloved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T04:42:10-07:00","id":1462990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462505-do-the-affects-of-blood-bonding-work-if-the-kindred-is-in-torpor?p=1462524#post1462524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The kind of situation that could lead into &amp;quot;the Bond loses its power when one is staked and enters torpor&amp;quot; misreading of anecdotal evidence previously discussed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Believe that is more due to the blood bond not being able to be renewed. If the person bound doesn't drink the bond does fade. And since the person bound can avoid the one in torpor a lot easier it is more likely to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T05:03:08-07:00","id":1462993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462505-do-the-affects-of-blood-bonding-work-if-the-kindred-is-in-torpor?p=1462990#post1462990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Believe that is more due to the blood bond not being able to be renewed. If the person bound doesn't drink the bond does fade. And since the person bound can avoid the one in torpor a lot easier it is more likely to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The bond diminishes, but for vampires, unlike with mortals &amp; ghouls, <b>does not</b> entirely fade with time, unless actively opposed. Choice and self-awareness are key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}